sedatives</article-title><source>J Neurotrauma</source><year>2007</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>S71</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17511550</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bratton</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Chestnut</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghajar</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>McConnell Hammond</surname><given-names>FF</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>OA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hartl</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Brain Trauma Foundation; American Association of Neurological Surgeons; Congress of Neurological Surgeons; Joint Section on Neurotrauma and Critical Care, AANS/CNS. Guidelines for the management of severe traumatic brain injury. XIII. Antiseizure prophylaxis</article-title><source>J Neurotrauma</source><year>2007</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>S83</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17511552</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bratton</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Chestnut</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghajar</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>McConnell Hammond</surname><given-names>FF</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>OA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hartl</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Brain Trauma Foundation; American Association of Neurological Surgeons; Congress of Neurological Surgeons; Joint Section on Neurotrauma and Critical Care, AANS/CNS. Guidelines for the management of severe traumatic brain inju